<title>BELGIUM: EU JOBLESS STEADY AT 10.9 PCT IN NOVEMBER.</title>
<headline>EU JOBLESS STEADY AT 10.9 PCT IN NOVEMBER.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union jobless figures</p>
<p>for November showed 18.2 million people out of work in the</p>
<p>15-country bloc, or 10.9 percent of the workforce, a figure</p>
<p>unchanged in the seven previous months, Eurostat said on Friday.</p>
<p>The EU statistics office said in a statement the largest</p>
<p>falls in jobless rates during the year to November were in</p>
<p>Britain (8.6 to 7.5), Denmark (6.6 to 5.5), Finland (16.2 to</p>
<p>15.3), Belgium (10 to 9.5) and Ireland (12.4 to 11.9).</p>
<p>During the same period, rates rose in Germany from 8.5 to</p>
<p>9.3 percent and in France from 11.8 to 12.5 percent.</p>
<p>Luxembourg's 3.3 percent rate and Austria's 4 percent pegged</p>
<p>the lower end of the EU league table in November while Spain's</p>
<p>stood at 22.3 percent and Finland's at 15.3 percent.</p>
<p>Eurostat gave no November figure for Greece, Italy or the</p>
<p>Netherlands.</p>
<p>It said U.S. unemployment amounted to 5.4 percent during the</p>
<p>same month and gave Japan's jobless for the previous month as</p>
<p>3.4 percent.</p>
<p>			 Nov'96   October'96</p>
<p>    EU average     10.9     10.9</p>
<p>    Luxembourg	3.3	3.2</p>
<p>    Austria	   4.0	4.1</p>
<p>    Denmark	   5.5	5.6</p>
<p>    Netherlands	--	6.4</p>
<p>    Portugal	  7.1	7.1</p>
<p>    Britain	   7.5	7.9</p>
<p>    Germany	   9.3	9.1</p>
<p>    Belgium	   9.5	9.6</p>
<p>    Sweden	   10.1     10.0</p>
<p>    Ireland	  11.9     12.1</p>
<p>    Italy		--	 --</p>
<p>    France	   12.5     12.4</p>
<p>    Finland	  15.3     15.0</p>
<p>    Spain	    22.3     22.3</p>
<p>    Greece	     --	 --</p>
</text>
